# Panic-on-input baseline migration log (#2111).
#
# The panic-input baseline (scripts/panic_input_baseline.json) is a DEBT list that may only
# shrink. The CI ratchet (check_no_panic_on_input.py --ratchet) fails any PR that GROWS the
# baseline UNLESS this file is changed in the same reviewed diff — each entry below is an
# explicit, human-reviewed acknowledgement that debt was intentionally added (e.g. bringing a
# new trust-boundary directory under coverage), not a new violation smuggled past the gate.
#
# Format: one dated entry per migration. Append only.

2026-07-21 (#2248, round 8): expand SCANNED_MODULES from a 6-file hand list to the full
attacker-controlled input surface at directory level — p2p/src, shared-protocol/src/mempool,
shared-protocol/src/cross_chain, native-chain/src/bin/launch_api (incl. the p2p_events peer
consumer that a prior review showed was invisible), execution-engine/src, sensor-attestation/src,
oracle-packet/src. Baseline grows from 29 to 303 pre-existing frozen fingerprints. This is
coverage expansion of existing code, not new violations; every added fingerprint is a
pre-existing site now brought under the gate. Future growth requires its own entry here.

2026-07-22 (#2248, round 36): the baseline's unit of identity changes from a
`path|rule|text` SET to a per-SITE fingerprint
`path|enclosing item|rule|normalized text|ordinal`.

Review of #2248 planted an attacker-controlled `.expect(...)` in a peer-payload function
reusing an existing same-file fingerprint: the gate reported `419 findings, 303 frozen,
0 NEW` and exited 0 with no baseline edit at all. Identical text was free. It is not now.

Every fingerprint below is a RE-KEYING of an already-frozen pre-existing site, not new
debt. Coverage was verified to strictly improve:

  * 13 production sites GAINED, previously invisible because the old `_in_test` scanned
    backwards 400 lines for `#[cfg(test)]`, so anything after a test module was exempt.
    Eight are in native-chain/src/bin/launch_api/p2p_events.rs — the peer consumer whose
    omission an earlier review had already flagged once.
  * 0 production sites lost. The dropped keys are all test code: p2p/src/tests/* (test-only
    files with no in-file marker, now excluded by path) and 73 inside launch_api/main.rs's
    `mod tests` (line >1436), each verified by line number rather than assumed.

Listing every fingerprint is the point. Authorization is per fingerprint now, so this log
is what a reviewer reads to see exactly which debt was accepted.

